      "thinking": "Let me analyze this certificate fragment.\n\nDocument-level info:\n- Certificate No: R49/2013-A-SK1-20.02 Rev. 1\n- Scheme: A (from \"OIML CERTIFICATE ISSUED UNDER SCHEME A\")\n- Member State: SLOVAKIA\n- Date issued: 6th November 2025 (from the signature date \"Date: 6th November 2025\")\n- OIML issuer ID: SK1 (from the certificate number, R49/2013-A-SK1-20.02 — SK1 indicates Slovakia issuing authority 1). Hmm, should I include it? The schema has oiml_issuer_id. The cert number contains SK1. I'll set it to \"SK1\".\n- Project number: maybe \"2025/ER010/SK1\"? That's the type evaluation report number. Project number — not explicitly present. The cert number pattern: R49/2013-A-SK1-20.02. Hmm, project number could be 20.02? Not certain. I'll omit project_number.\n- Page total: 10 (from \"Page 1 of 10 pages\")\n\nIssuing authority:\n- Name: Slovak Legal Metrology (SLM)\n- Address lines: Geologická 9966/1, 821 06 Bratislava-Podunajské Biskupice, Slovakia; Product Certification Body, Hviedzoslavova 31, 974 01 Banská Bystrica, Slovakia\n- Person responsible: Dušan Šmigura, Director of PCB → person_responsible: \"Dušan Šmigura\", person_title: \"Director of PCB\"\n\nApplicants:\n- Ningbo Aimei Meter Manufacture Co., Ltd., 68, West Town Road, Shangtian Town, Fenghua, Zhejiang, China 3155 (note: address shows \"China 3155\" — probably truncated postal code, keep as-is)\n\nManufacturers:\n- Same as applicant.\n\nCertified type:\n- Category: \"Water meter\" (Water meter type UWM)\n- type_designations: [\"UWM\"]\n- module_designation: \"Ultrasonic water meter intended for the metering of cold potable water\" — hmm, this is under \"Designation of the module (if applicable)\". The section gives a description, not a module like \"Analog load cell\". Could set it to that string, or null. The schema says module_designation: \"Analog load cell\" | \"Not applicable\" | null. Since a designation is provided, I'll include the text.\n- description: The ultrasonic water meter type UWM designed to measure... I'll compose a description from section 1 and 2.\n\nModel family:\n- Models: DN15, DN20 mentioned in revision history (\"plastic body for DN15 and DN20\"). But the fragment doesn't give the full model matrix (tables in point 3 not shown — \"batteries see tables in point 3\" but point 3 is not in this fragment). There's mention of brass body and plastic body, temperature classes T30, T50, T70. This suggests variants. But the fragment doesn't include the actual model tables. Should I include model_family? The revision history mentions DN15 and DN20. Hmm, but I don't have full info. Rule: include ONLY if cert covers >1 model variant. We know it covers DN15 and DN20 at least. I could add models [{\"model_id\": \"DN15\"}, {\"model_id\": \"DN20\"}]. But is it safe? The revision history says \"plastic body for DN15 and DN20 with temperature class T30 and T50\". Also brass body with T70. It's plausible. However, parts 2-4 of the certificate probably contain the detailed tables. Since this is \"for the content present in THIS fragment only\", I could include the model family with DN15 and DN20 based on what's stated. I think it's reasonable to include model_family with DN15/DN20 models. But maybe cautious: include only if clearly multiple models. The revision history clearly indicates DN15 and DN20 exist as sizes. I'll include them.\n\nActually, let me be careful — fabricating is discouraged. DN15 and DN20 are explicitly mentioned. I'll include model_family with models DN15, DN20.\n\nComponents:\n- Flow sensor: role \"flow_sensor\", described as cylindrical brass body or plastic body...\n- Calculator and indication device: role \"calculator_and_indication_device\"\n- Non-essential: non-return valve (optional), communication interfaces. Could include as components with alternatives \"OR\"? The communication interfaces list: optical infrared, RF, LoRaWAN, wM-Bus, OMS, Sigfox, NB-IoT, M-Bus, Pulse — these are options. Maybe record as characteristics instead: communication_interfaces with value list of strings.\n\nI'll add components for flow sensor and calculator/indication device with characteristics embedded (body material: brass OR plastic).\n\nCharacteristics type_level:\n- accuracy_class: 2 (from \"For accuracy class (if applicable): 2\") — this goes to recommendation.accuracy_classes as well. Actually accuracy class belongs to recommendation.accuracy_classes = [\"2\"]. Could also be in characteristics but schema puts it in recommendation.\n- battery: two or three non-replaceable lithium batteries, Umax=3.7V, life up to 16 years; one non-replaceable lithium battery, Umax=3.6V, life up to 10 years. These are alternatives. Could put in characteristics config_level or components. Hmm. I could put battery characteristics as config_level entries: attribute \"number_of_batteries\" axis \"battery_configuration\" values: {condition: \"2 or 3 non-replaceable lithium batteries\", value: {min:2,max:3}}... That might be overkill. Simpler: type_level characteristic \"battery\" value string? Rule 2 says structured values strictly; value can be a string. I could do:\n\nconfig_level: [\n  {attribute: \"number_of_lithium_batteries\", axis: \"battery_option\", values: [{condition: \"non-replaceable lithium batteries, Umax 3.7 V, lifetime up to 16 years\", value: {min:2, max:3}}, {condition: \"non-replaceable lithium battery, Umax 3.6 V, lifetime up to 10 years\", value: 1}]},\n  {attribute: \"battery_voltage_max\", axis: \"battery_option\", values: [{condition: \"two or three batteries\", value: 3.7, unit \"V\"}, {condition: \"one battery\", value: 3.6, unit \"V\"}]},\n  {attribute: \"battery_lifetime\", ...}\n]\n\nThat's a bit verbose but captures it. Alternatively components entry for battery. I'll do config_level.\n\n- display: LCD non-permanent display, 10 digits, indication range 99999.99999 m³. Characteristic: \"max_indication_range\" value 99999.99999 unit m³. Digits: 10.\n- measurement_principle: \"ultrasonic bidirectional transit-time\" — string value. Could include as type_level characteristic: {\"value\": \"ultrasonic bidirectional transit-time\"}. Good.\n- installation_positions: all positions. Not designed to measure reverse flow → reverse_flow: false? Could add \"reverse_flow_measurement\": {value: false}? Hmm, careful not to fabricate — it says \"not designed to measure the reverse flow\". I could add characteristic \"reverse_flow\" value \"not measured\". Maybe skip; keep description covers it.\n\nTemperature classes: T30, T50 (plastic body DN15, DN20), T70 (brass body). These are config-level. I could add config_level entries: attribute \"temperature_class\", axis \"body_material_and_size\", values: [{condition: \"brass body\", value: \"T70\"}, {condition: \"plastic body DN15 and DN20\", value: \"T30 and T50\"}]. Value \"T30 and T50\" is a string list. Hmm. I'll include as strings: \"T30, T50\". Fine.\n\nAlso \"Ratio to R800\" mentioned in revision history — not a characteristic value here. Checksum 25667 — revision change note.\n\nRecommendation:\n- id: \"R49\" (canonical), edition: 2013, amendment: null, scheme: \"A\", accuracy_classes: [\"2\"]. Accuracy class 2 — is it a string or number? Class \"2\" for water meters. Could be number 2. Schema says accuracy_classes[] — I'll use [2]? Hmm. Class designations can be like \"2\" or \"U\". Safer as string \"2\"? For R49 classes are 1 and 2. I'll use [2] as number... Actually class labels are identifiers, strings make more sense. I'll use [\"2\"].\n\nTest reports:\n- id: \"2025/ER010/SK1\", date: \"2025-11-06\" or \"6th November 2025\", pages: 19, role: \"type_evaluation_report\"\n- documentation file: \"Ningbo Aimei_UWM_01\", date 6th November 2025, pages: 76, role: \"documentation_file\"\n\nRevision history:\n- revision \"0\", date \"17rd July 2020\" (typo in source; I'd write \"17 July 2020\"? Better keep as given \"17rd July 2020\"? Hmm, it's a typo of 17th. I'll normalize to \"17 July 2020\" or keep original. I'll keep the date as \"2020-07-17\" normalized. Actually rules don't say to normalize dates. I'll use ISO dates: \"2020-07-17\" and \"2025-11-06\". The date_issued: \"2025-11-06\".\n- revision \"1\", date 2025-11-06, changes: list of adds and changes. changes field is a string. I'll concatenate with newlines or \"; \". The schema shows `changes` — I'll write a combined string.\n\nFootnotes: none present.\n\nCertificate number: \"R49/2013-A-SK1-20.02 Rev. 1\" — should number include \"Rev. 1\"? The field is \"number\". I'll use \"R49/2013-A-SK1-20.02\" and maybe note revision in revision_history. But the displayed number includes Rev. 1. Hmm. The number field: \"R49/2013-A-SK1-20.02 Rev. 1\". I'll include the full as displayed? The revision history captures rev. I think keeping the full string as printed is safest for certificate.number. Actually many extractors keep number without revision. The header repeats \"R49/2013-A-SK1-20.02 Rev. 1\". I'll set number: \"R49/2013-A-SK1-20.02\" and revision is implied in revision_history... but there's no separate revision field at certificate level. Hmm. To be faithful, include \"R49/2013-A-SK1-20.02 Rev. 1\"? I'll go with the full string as it appears, since that's the certificate number as printed. Actually, I think number should be the canonical identifier; the rev is part of it here. I'll include \"R49/2013-A-SK1-20.02 Rev. 1\".\n\nPage_total: 10.\n\nOIML issuer id: \"SK1\". From cert number \"-SK1-\". I'll include it for certificate and issuing_authority.\n\nAddress lines for issuing authority:\n- \"Geologická 9966/1\"\n- \"821 06 Bratislava-Podunajské Biskupice\"\n- \"Slovakia\"\n- \"Product Certification Body\"\n- \"Hviedzoslavova 31\"\n- \"974 01 Banská Bystrica\"\n- \"Slovakia\"\n\nApplicant address:\n- \"68, West Town Road, Shangtian Town\"\n- \"Fenghua\"\n- \"Zhejiang, China 3155\"\n\nHmm the OCR shows \"Zhejiang, China 3155\" — postal code likely 315500 truncated. Keep as printed: \"Zhejiang, China 3155\".\n\nCategory: schema examples list categories like \"Load cell\", \"Gas meter\"... For water meter: \"Water meter\".\n\nDescription: compose from sections 1 and 2. I'll write a concise description.\n\nNow characteristics:\n\ntype_level:\n- measuring_principle: {\"value\": \"ultrasonic bidirectional transit-time\", unit null}\n- display_digits: 10\n- max_indication_range: 99999.99999, unit \"m³\" (unit_symbol \"m³\"; unit_id maybe \"u:unit_of_volume\"? Leave null per rule: leave null unless certain. m³ could be \"u:cubic_metre\" — I'm fairly certain unitsdb has \"u:m3\"? Not certain of exact ID; leave null.)\n- display_time_volume_shown: 10 s (\"The measured volume is displayed for 10 s\") — characteristic \"display_duration_of_measured_volume\": 10 s. Maybe include.\n- communication_interfaces: value string list: \"optical infrared, RF, LoRaWAN, wM-Bus, OMS, Sigfox, NB-IoT, M-Bus, Pulse\" — as a string value. Or array? Value must be number | {min,max} | string. So a single string. I'll join with \", \".\n- optional_non_return_valve: true? Could do {\"value\": \"optional\"}. Maybe skip; description covers.\n\nconfig_level for battery:\naxis \"battery_configuration\":\n- number_of_batteries: [{condition: \"non-replaceable lithium batteries (Umax 3.7 V, lifetime up to 16 years)\", value: {min: 2, max: 3}}, {condition: \"non-replaceable lithium battery (Umax 3.6 V, lifetime up to 10 years)\", value: 1}]\n- battery_nominal_voltage: [{condition: \"two or three batteries\", value: 3.7, unit V}, {condition: \"one battery\", value: 3.6}]\n- battery_lifetime: [{condition \"two or three batteries\", value {min: null, max: 16}, unit \"years\"? symbol \"a\" or \"years\"}, {condition \"one battery\", max 10}]\n\nHmm, maybe simpler to structure per condition:\n\nconfig_level: [\n {\n   \"attribute\": \"battery_configuration\",\n   \"axis\": \"battery_option\",\n   \"values\": [\n     {\"condition\": \"two or three non-replaceable lithium batteries\", \"value\": ...}\n   ]\n }\n]\n\nActually the config values follow {condition, value, unit_symbol}. Let me create separate config_level entries per attribute with axis \"battery_option\" and conditions \"option_1: two or three lithium batteries\" vs \"option_2: one lithium battery\". Cleaner:\n\n[\n  {\"attribute\": \"number_of_batteries\", \"axis\": \"battery_option\", \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"lithium batteries, Umax 3.7 V, lifetime up to 16 years\", \"value\": {\"min\": 2, \"max\": 3}},\n    {\"condition\": \"lithium battery, Umax 3.6 V, lifetime up to 10 years\", \"value\": 1}\n  ]},\n  {\"attribute\": \"battery_max_voltage\", \"axis\": \"battery_option\", \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"two or three batteries\", \"value\": 3.7, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"one battery\", \"value\": 3.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"V\"}\n  ]},\n  {\"attribute\": \"battery_lifetime_max\", \"axis\": \"battery_option\", \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"two or three batteries\", \"value\": 16, \"unit_symbol\": \"years\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"one battery\", \"value\": 10, \"unit_symbol\": \"years\"}\n  ]}\n]\n\nAnd temperature class config:\n[\n  {\"attribute\": \"temperature_class\", \"axis\": \"body_material_and_size\", \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"brass body\", \"value\": \"T70\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"plastic body, DN15 and DN20\", \"value\": \"T30 and T50\"}\n  ]}\n]\n\nHmm the T30/T50 for plastic — from revision history \"plastic body for DN15 and DN20 with temperature class T30 and T50\". Could be T30 and T50 both available. Value string \"T30, T50\".\n\nWait — this info comes from the revision history changes. It describes what Rev 1 added. It's legitimately part of the certificate content. I'll include but the conditions are as described.\n\nActually, should I be more careful? The detailed tables in point 3 (not in this fragment) would give the authoritative matrix. But the fragment does state these facts. I'll include them.\n\nModel family:\n{\n  \"family_name\": \"UWM\",\n  \"models\": [{\"model_id\": \"DN15\"}, {\"model_id\": \"DN20\"}]\n}\nFamily name: the type is UWM; models DN15/DN20 sizes. I'll set family_name \"UWM\".\n\nComponents:\n- role: \"flow_sensor\", type_designations: null? No type designation given. characteristics: {\"body_material\": [\"brass\", \"plastic\"] with alternatives OR, \"connections\": \"inlet and outlet threaded\"}. The schema components characteristics{} is a free object. I'll do:\n  {\"role\": \"flow_sensor\", \"characteristics\": {\"body\": \"cylindrical brass body or plastic body (alternatives)\", \"connections\": \"inlet and outlet threaded\", \"measurement_element\": \"inner plastic element with two mirrors (sound path)\", \"sensors\": \"two ultrasonic sensors placed on the upside of the cylindrical body\"}}\n- role: \"calculator_and_indication_device\", characteristics: {\"housing\": \"plastic housing directly mounted on the flow sensor\", \"display\": \"electronic LCD non-permanent (automatic scrolling) display with 10 digits\", \"indication_range_max\": 99999.99999 m³...}\n\nMaybe keep characteristics in components simpler and put numeric ones in type_level. I'll include both appropriately.\n\nmatrix_tables: none in this fragment (tables in point 3 not present).\n\nFootnotes: none.\n\nNow output JSON.\n\ncertificate:\n{\n  \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-SK1-20.02 Rev. 1\",\n  \"scheme\": \"A\",\n  \"project_number\": null — omit.\n  \"page_total\": 10,\n  \"member_state\": \"Slovakia\",\n  \"date_issued\": \"2025-11-06\",\n  \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"SK1\"\n}\n\nissuing_authority:\n{\n  \"name\": \"Slovak Legal Metrology (SLM)\",\n  \"address_lines\": [\n    \"Geologická 9966/1\",\n    \"821 06 Bratislava-Podunajské Biskupice\",\n    \"Slovakia\",\n    \"Product Certification Body\",\n    \"Hviedzoslavova 31\",\n    \"974 01 Banská Bystrica\",\n    \"Slovakia\"\n  ],\n  \"person_responsible\": \"Dušan Šmigura\",\n  \"person_title\": \"Director of PCB\",\n  \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"SK1\"\n}\n\napplicants, manufacturers as above.\n\ncertified_type:\n{\n  \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n  \"type_designations\": [\"UWM\"],\n  \"module_designation\": \"Ultrasonic water meter intended for the metering of cold potable water\",\n  \"description\": \"Compact ultrasonic water meter with electronic indication device designed to measure, memorise and display the volume of cold potable water passing through the measurement transducer at metering conditions; measurement based on ultrasonic bidirectional transit-time principle; can be installed in all positions; not designed to measure reverse flow. Essential parts: flow sensor (cylindrical brass or plastic body with threaded connections, inner plastic element with two mirrors/sound paths, two ultrasonic sensors) and calculator with indication device (plastic housing directly mounted on flow sensor, main PCB with LCD display and optical sensor, non-replaceable lithium batteries). Optional: non-return valve; communication interfaces: optical infrared, RF, LoRaWAN, wM-Bus, OMS, Sigfox, NB-IoT, M-Bus, Pulse.\"\n}\n\nmodel_family as above.\n\ncomponents as above.\n\ncharacteristics:\ntype_level:\n- \"measuring_principle\": {\"value\": \"ultrasonic bidirectional transit-time\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null}\n- \"display_digits\": {\"value\": 10, ...}\n- \"maximum_indication_range\": {\"value\": 99999.99999, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\"}\n- \"display_duration_of_measured_volume\": {\"value\": 10, \"unit_symbol\": \"s\"}\n- \"communication_interfaces\": {\"value\": \"optical infrared, RF, LoRaWAN, wM-Bus, OMS, Sigfox, NB-IoT, M-Bus, Pulse\"}\n- \"installation_positions\": {\"value\": \"all positions\"}\n\nmodel_level: none (no numeric per-model data in fragment; DN15/DN20 don't have varying attributes here besides temp class which is config). Actually temperature class varies by body material + size — that's config_level.\n\nconfig_level: battery + temperature class.\n\nrecommendation:\n{\"id\": \"R49\", \"edition\": 2013, \"scheme\": \"A\", \"accuracy_classes\": [\"2\"]}\n\ntest_reports:\n[\n {\"id\": \"2025/ER010/SK1\", \"date\": \"2025-11-06\", \"pages\": 19, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n {\"id\": \"Ningbo Aimei_UWM_01\", \"date\": \"2025-11-06\", \"pages\": 76, \"role\": \"documentation_file\"}\n]\n\nrevision_history:\n[\n {\"revision\": \"0\", \"date\": \"2020-07-17\", \"changes\": \"Certificate first issued\"},\n {\"revision\": \"1\", \"date\": \"2025-11-06\", \"changes\": \"Add: ratio to R800; temperature class T70 for brass body; checksum 25667; options of trademarks (6 pcs); plastic body for DN15 and DN20 with temperature class T30 and T50. Changes: one pc battery to 2 or 3 pcs batteries; address of OIML Issuing Authority SLM; formal the year \\\"2020\\\" to \\\"20\\\" in the Certificate number\"}\n]\n\nNote the original says \"17rd July 2020\" — typo. Normalize to 2020-07-17.\n\nNo footnotes.\n\nOutput a single JSON object. Ensure valid JSON, no trailing commas. Use \"m³\" unicode fine.\n\nOne more: \"checksum 25667\" — could be a characteristic? It's from revision changes; skip as characteristic.\n\n\"Ratio to R800\" — R800 is a controlled document? Actually R800? No — for water meters, temperature class T70 relates to... Hmm \"Ratio to R800\" maybe referencing pressure loss? Skip.\n\nLet me write the JSON.",
